Say when a table asks its data source, and what it hears.

iA Writer adds a custom pattern and no row appears. The action is delivered, which cocotron 0140
and the correction after it established, so the question was whether the table ever reloads and
what its data source says when it does.

-[NSTableView numberOfRows] caches in _numberOfRows and answers from the cache until something
clears it, so from outside a table that never reloads and a data source that answers zero are
indistinguishable. Two traces separate them, and between them they cover every runtime path:
noteNumberOfRowsChanged is the ONLY runtime invalidation, reached from reloadData, which
reloadDataForRowIndexes, insertRowsAtIndexes, removeRowsAtIndexes and moveRowAtIndex all call; and
numberOfRows prints only when it actually asks, so a redraw does not flood the log.

MEASURED, and the drive carries its own control because a second table of the same class is on
screen at the same time:

    CIDER_ROWS ask IATableView source=IACustomPatternsTableViewController -> 0     5 times
    CIDER_ROWS ask IATableView source=Writer.LibraryTreeViewController    -> 5    24 times

Five is exactly the number of files the library list shows in the capture. So the table machinery
reloads, asks, believes the answer and draws it, demonstrably, in the same process and the same
class as the one that stays empty.

THE CUSTOM PATTERNS TABLE IS NOT THE DEFECT. It invalidates and asks five times and hears zero
every time, so addPattern: runs, the reload happens, and the application has no pattern to show.
Whatever fails is inside the application between the action and its model, and it is not this
table, not the row cache, and not the data source protocol.

